{"cluster_id": "C-2293", "topic": "The byte-weighted manifest decode cache remains keyed by", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B008-098"], "canonical_claim": "The byte-weighted manifest decode cache remains keyed by `(ManifestId, Token)`; a token mismatch causes a fresh `GET` and decode, a failed decode is not cached, and the mandatory manifest `HEAD` remains.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-08-cas-part-folder-cache-design.md#acceptance-criteria"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2294", "topic": "When the destination ref is absent, republishRef retains", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B009-022"], "canonical_claim": "When the destination ref is absent, republishRef retains the normal stageManifest \u2192 precommitAdd \u2192 promote \u2192 dropRef sequence.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-08-cas-promote-over-committed-leak-fix-design.md##fix-1c"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2295", "topic": "The obsolete ref handoff transfers a contiguous writer-log", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B010-037"], "canonical_claim": "The obsolete ref handoff transfers a contiguous writer-log prefix into the GC generation through the existing single `gc/state` CAS; before that CAS the prefix is authoritative, and after it the GC fold is authoritative.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-ref-snapshot-log-design.md#summary"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2296", "topic": "dropNamespace is represented as one constant-size remove_namespace transaction", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B010-040"], "canonical_claim": "`dropNamespace` is represented as one constant-size `remove_namespace` transaction that atomically clears committed and precommit bindings and changes the incarnation to `Removed`; it does not serialize the owner list.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-ref-snapshot-log-design.md#summary"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2297", "topic": "A writer-log object can be removed only when", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B010-043"], "canonical_claim": "A writer-log object can be removed only when the adopted fold seal names a valid `RefBaseSet` whose namespace row has the same incarnation and `folded_seq >= log_record.seq`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-ref-snapshot-log-design.md#core-invariants"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2298", "topic": "Every writer-log key and GC ref-fold entry contains", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B010-045"], "canonical_claim": "Every writer-log key and GC ref-fold entry contains the namespace incarnation, so an older incarnation cannot cover or consume a newer incarnation's sequence numbers.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-ref-snapshot-log-design.md#core-invariants"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2299", "topic": "remove_namespace changes Live to Removed and clears every", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B010-047"], "canonical_claim": "`remove_namespace` changes `Live` to `Removed` and clears every owner binding in one replay transition; no later mutation is valid for that incarnation.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-ref-snapshot-log-design.md#core-invariants"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2300", "topic": "A warm-cache isolated ref mutation creates one _log", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B010-049"], "canonical_claim": "A warm-cache isolated ref mutation creates one `_log` object and performs zero ref-state reads, while a compatible batch of `B` mutations shares one `putIfAbsent`; uncertain writes are resolved by an exact-key `GET`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-ref-snapshot-log-design.md#core-invariants"]}
